{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "זאת תורת הנזיר", :translit "zot torat ha-nazir", :gloss "this is the law of the nazirite"} {:he "תורת נזרו", :translit "torat nizro", :gloss "the law of his nazirite-vow"} {:he "עבודה", :translit "avodah", :gloss "divine service"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut of parashiyot: זאת תורת הנזיר follows the passage of wine-grape prohibitions; Priestly Blessing follows nazirite passage"}], :frame {:text "Rabbi Yehudah derives that a scholar who drank wine may not render halakhic decisions, likening it to a priest who drank wine entering the Temple, at Eruvin 64a. The Gemara states that a priest intoxicated with wine is disqualified from the Priestly Blessing at Ta'anit 26b. The Priestly Blessing is called avodah at Shabbat 119a. Scripture juxtaposes the nazirite passage to the Priestly Blessing immediately following in Numbers 6:24.", :sources ["Eruvin 64a" "Ta'anit 26b" "Shabbat 119a" "Numbers 6:24"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut of parashiyot: זאת תורת הנזיר follows the passage of wine-grape prohibitions; Priestly Blessing follows nazirite passage", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:14.547592497Z", :model "glm-5.2"}